    "created_at": "2022-04-22T18:33:10Z",
    "updated_at": "2022-04-22T18:34:42Z",
    "body": "This sounds like an implementation issue with screen reader software, which is best filed on their issue trackers. If they are announcing things on page load or on focus, but that is giving a bad experience, then they should not do that. (There is nothing in the spec that requires them to announce at specific times.)\r\n\r\nIn particular, your claims that this is because browsers/screen readers are following the spec, such as\r\n\r\n> Technically, the browser is doing its job correctly here as it is respecting the spec.\r\n\r\nand\r\n\r\n> Why does it perform double duty? My guess is because Chrome is following what is defined in the HTML Spec.\r\n\r\ndon't appear to be correct, as there are no accessibility mappings or screen reader behaviors defined in the HTML spec.",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
    "pin": null,
