    "updated_at": "2022-04-24T19:37:14Z",
    "body": "I do think that the HTML specification could be changed. Namely, as it is written in the specification for [minlength](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/form-control-infrastructure.html#attr-fe-minlength): The field is only evaluated as invalid if the user has made an entry and never initially if, for example, a too short entry has been made by value or script. If this is done for all other invalid checks (pattern, required, type=email, type=URL etc.) this would be the simplest solution for the problems described here. All other solutions have already been discussed extensively and seem to be impossible or difficult to implement.\r\n",
    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
    "pin": null,
