    "created_at": "2022-04-24T22:11:42Z",
    "updated_at": "2022-04-24T22:11:42Z",
    "body": "> The thing that seems to be the problem here is that the screen reader is jumping the gun and yelling HEY THIS FORM IS INVALID just because there's a page that happens to have a form on it, when the user doesn't yet have a reason to care about the form's validity state.\r\n\r\nI suggest its the Browser accessibility layer that is doing the jumping, the screen reader is just reporting what is exposed in the acc tree.",
