    "created_at": "2022-04-24T22:31:17Z",
    "updated_at": "2022-04-24T22:31:32Z",
    "body": "I think I'm seeing the mismatch now... a form field that's in the invalid state as an HTML form field isn't necessarily `aria-invalid` because of that fact. \r\n\r\nThe ARIA spec says `aria-invalid` \"Indicates the entered value does not conform to the format expected by the application\", which can be read as requiring there to be an \"entered\" value present. This reading is backed up by: \"When the user attempts to submit data involving a field for which [aria-required](https://w3c.github.io/aria/#aria-required) is true, authors MAY use the [aria-invalid](https://w3c.github.io/aria/#aria-invalid) attribute to signal there is an error. However, if the user has not attempted to submit the form, authors SHOULD NOT set the aria-invalid attribute on required [widgets](https://w3c.github.io/aria/#dfn-widget) simply because the user has not yet entered data.\"",
    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
